WEBVTT

01:49.389 --> 01:52.896
CLOSED

02:12.310 --> 02:14.607
She always had a death wish.

02:16.903 --> 02:19.324
<i>Sure, she put up a hell of a front.</i>

02:19.324 --> 02:21.788
<i>But every time she came over to my cell,</i>

02:21.788 --> 02:24.793
<i>she had reservations about killing to stay alive.</i>

02:25.169 --> 02:27.800
<i>Sayin’ she’d probably be better off dead.</i>

02:29.887 --> 02:31.766
So I told her,

02:32.016 --> 02:37.945
“If ya wanna die that bad, then once I get outta here
you’ll be on the top of my hit list.”

02:39.573 --> 02:40.784
It was a joke, of course.

02:42.286 --> 02:44.374
<i>Omigosh, I will?
It’s a promise, then!</i>

02:46.461 --> 02:51.054
<i>But looking back on it...
I think she really felt that way.</i>

02:52.181 --> 02:54.770
Your unluck helped save Gena, kid.

02:55.312 --> 02:56.356
You’ve got my thanks.

02:58.695 --> 02:59.697
Andy.

03:00.239 --> 03:01.116
Yeah?

03:01.951 --> 03:03.328
I have a favor to ask.

03:05.082 --> 03:07.044
Can’t we make a change?

03:07.044 --> 03:10.050
So that no one else suffers like Ms. Gena did...

03:10.050 --> 03:12.514
Can’t the two of us change the Union?

03:12.806 --> 03:14.852
All right! Count me in!

03:15.269 --> 03:18.526
Makes it easier to charm the pants off ya.

03:18.526 --> 03:20.237
Y-You mean it?

03:21.782 --> 03:24.454
You really think we can do it?

03:24.705 --> 03:27.836
The Union’s welcome wagon should be here soon.

03:27.836 --> 03:30.132
First order of business is scoping out
the joint from the inside.

03:33.556 --> 03:35.476
Anyhoo, let’s toast to the dead.

03:35.476 --> 03:38.440
Right... to Ms. Gena!

03:38.440 --> 03:39.317
Yeah.

03:41.572 --> 03:43.158
Now, then...

03:43.534 --> 03:44.828
- Bottoms...
- Bottoms...

03:45.120 --> 03:45.705
...up?

03:45.789 --> 03:47.166
IX, X.

03:47.166 --> 03:48.961
I have come to pick you up.

03:48.961 --> 03:50.590
Well, y’got here sooner than I expected!

04:01.821 --> 04:03.156
Wait, is this...

04:03.448 --> 04:03.991
Andy!

04:05.912 --> 04:06.997
Whoa! What are you doing?

04:07.081 --> 04:08.584
Sayin’ hello.

04:08.668 --> 04:09.377
Huh?

04:10.170 --> 04:11.924
Let’s off these losers!

04:24.575 --> 04:27.789
You guys woulda saved us all some time
if ya had just dropped dead.

04:27.789 --> 04:29.793
Guess that was wishful thinkin’, eh?

04:31.505 --> 04:33.467
See? Aren’t they interesting?

04:33.760 --> 04:35.680
You two are just as the reports detailed.

04:35.680 --> 04:37.768
Undead... and Unluck.

04:37.768 --> 04:39.395
Welcome to the Union.

04:39.772 --> 04:41.734
JUIZ

04:43.236 --> 04:45.157
SHEN

04:47.036 --> 04:48.998
BILLY

04:50.627 --> 04:52.547
PHIL

04:54.676 --> 04:56.555
TATIANA

04:58.935 --> 05:00.855
ISSHIN

05:02.943 --> 05:04.863
TOP

05:07.034 --> 05:09.080
NICO

05:10.583 --> 05:12.378
FUKO‎
ANDY

05:12.879 --> 05:14.967
Ayy, sick! Wicked sick!

05:25.822 --> 05:27.576
Cool it, Tatiana.

05:27.659 --> 05:30.038
He killed Ms. Gena!

05:32.251 --> 05:35.967
Yeah, I know. But fighting among members
is strictly forbidden.

05:35.967 --> 05:36.886
But!

05:36.969 --> 05:39.056
I see at least one
of ‘em’s got a quick temper.

05:39.056 --> 05:39.850
Huh?

05:44.400 --> 05:45.444
Why, you lousy...

05:45.778 --> 05:46.989
Stop this.

05:50.245 --> 05:52.416
Huh? Is it hot in here?

05:52.709 --> 05:56.132
<i>My hand’s... actin’ on its own?</i>

05:57.217 --> 06:01.184
I’m sorry, Boss!
Please, I don’t want to kill Mr. Billy!

06:01.184 --> 06:03.146
Huh? I’m going to die?

06:03.146 --> 06:05.025
What about you, Undead?

06:05.777 --> 06:09.325
You win. I give up.
Just make it stop, okay?

06:10.035 --> 06:11.496
How very noble.

06:13.751 --> 06:16.799
Hey, sorry about all that...
but it got us results.

06:18.218 --> 06:19.345
Uh, right.

06:20.767 --> 06:23.272
AUGUST 6TH

06:23.272 --> 06:25.777
MIDNIGHT

06:27.280 --> 06:29.910
Could you maybe stop with the sudden surprises?

06:29.910 --> 06:31.831
What’s the point if it ain’t sudden?

06:34.460 --> 06:36.381
I take it we’re all seated now?

06:37.300 --> 06:39.429
Let us proceed. Apocalypse.

06:44.147 --> 06:45.525
Fresh blood, huh?

06:46.359 --> 06:48.030
Apocalypse.

06:51.411 --> 06:53.624
Quest Open!

07:02.642 --> 07:05.064
There are six quests this time.

07:05.732 --> 07:07.485
Quest one:

07:07.736 --> 07:15.209
Capture of the UMA Burn. Participant count: six.
Addition of eleventh seat.

07:16.377 --> 07:17.839
Quest two:

07:18.090 --> 07:25.939
Capture of the UMA Eat. Participant count: five.
Location of Negator Unburn.

07:29.655 --> 07:31.366
Quest three:

07:31.909 --> 07:39.967
Neutralization of UMA Language. Participant count: one.
Unification of all world languages.

07:42.179 --> 07:47.148
Quests... so this is the quota
that Gena mentioned.

07:47.148 --> 07:50.320
So, um... what is that thing talking about?

07:50.320 --> 07:54.162
We’re gathering intel for now.
Just try to retain as much of the conversation as possible.

07:54.162 --> 07:55.372
O-Okay.

07:57.627 --> 07:59.715
Quest four:

07:59.715 --> 08:03.346
Capture of Negator Unseen.

08:08.273 --> 08:13.784
Participation count: one.
Location of UMA Call.

08:14.578 --> 08:16.414
Quest five:

08:16.414 --> 08:18.460
Capture of UMA Past.

08:20.798 --> 08:26.936
Participation count: three.
Location of Artifact Rebellion.

08:27.394 --> 08:29.357
Quest six:

08:29.775 --> 08:38.500
Capture of UMA Spoil. Participation count: three.
Location of Negator Unrepair.

08:42.091 --> 08:49.982
You have until August 31st.
If all quests are not fulfilled, the penalty will be...

08:51.401 --> 08:54.323
...the addition of UMA Galaxy!

08:55.577 --> 08:57.539
Now, choose!

08:58.081 --> 08:59.710
What does he mean by “Galaxy”?

08:59.710 --> 09:02.674
No clue. Save the questions
for later and pay attention.

09:02.674 --> 09:03.718
O-Oh, okay.

09:04.051 --> 09:07.767
Nico. Run an analysis on this data
along with our own.

09:08.686 --> 09:09.688
Aye.

09:14.280 --> 09:16.910
Aah! There it is! I see now!

09:17.286 --> 09:20.793
Looks like what we can handle now
are the first three.

09:20.793 --> 09:24.676
Thanks to investigators, we already know
the UMA habitats and how to counter them.

09:26.304 --> 09:30.479
Burn should take highest priority since
the reward is the most worthwhile.

09:30.563 --> 09:33.026
Addition of 11th seat.

09:33.527 --> 09:36.282
We should give up on the last one.

09:36.282 --> 09:39.163
We’re severely lacking in relevant data.
We’d only lose our members.

09:39.665 --> 09:45.342
Very well. Then, we’ll first mobilize all members
toward clearing quests one, two, and three.

09:45.635 --> 09:47.471
We’ll accept the penalty.

09:47.471 --> 09:50.268
This time we’ll focus
on strengthening our forces.

09:52.314 --> 09:54.861
Now then, we’ll divide the quests among us.

09:55.195 --> 09:56.322
U-Um, excuse me.

09:56.406 --> 09:57.282
Hm?

09:57.534 --> 09:59.161
Would you mind explaining what that book is?

09:59.871 --> 10:01.374
You talking to me?

10:01.667 --> 10:02.836
Yes, yes!

10:04.506 --> 10:09.014
That’s Apocalypse,
the first Artifact found on Earth.

10:10.518 --> 10:12.229
APOCALYPSE‎
THE FIRST ARTIFACT FOUND ON EARTH‎

10:12.312 --> 10:15.987
When Negators sit in every seat
at the Roundtable, it opens...

10:17.532 --> 10:19.995
...and forces a bunch of unreasonable tasks on us.

10:19.995 --> 10:21.122
If we clear them,
we get a reward.

10:21.749 --> 10:24.420
But if we fail,
we get hit with a penalty.

10:27.134 --> 10:29.848
I see... but do we have to do what it says?

10:31.852 --> 10:33.647
Is it worth doing, even if...

10:34.064 --> 10:35.860
...we just end up getting hurt?

10:36.820 --> 10:38.699
Ms. Gena said it herself.

10:38.699 --> 10:44.084
No matter how hard she tried,
nothing ever changed, and she suffered as a result.

10:44.544 --> 10:48.552
So tell me-are that book’s instructions
really worth all that trouble?

10:49.220 --> 10:52.977
And that fourth quest said to capture a Negator.

10:53.394 --> 10:56.860
Are you going to treat more people
like how you treated me and Andy?

10:57.361 --> 11:01.410
Outside of having abilities,
we’re just normal people!

11:02.079 --> 11:06.922
And the same goes for all of you, right?

11:06.922 --> 11:09.845
I don’t know what’s going on here,
but this needs to stop no-

11:09.928 --> 11:11.305
Ninety-eight times.

11:12.850 --> 11:15.438
That is the number of times Rules
have been added to Earth.

11:16.567 --> 11:17.694
<i>Sex.</i>

11:18.571 --> 11:19.614
<i>Language.</i>

11:20.616 --> 11:21.660
<i>Race.</i>

11:22.579 --> 11:23.454
<i>Death.</i>

11:24.583 --> 11:25.668
<i>Sickness.</i>

11:26.294 --> 11:28.172
These are but a single handful.

11:28.716 --> 11:32.472
Once every three months,
new penalties are added even without our intervention.

11:33.433 --> 11:34.894
Which is why we intervene.

11:36.857 --> 11:39.613
Our forces must be strong enough
to complete these quests.

11:39.613 --> 11:43.077
To accomplish this,
we capture and utilize those with power.

11:43.621 --> 11:46.250
By gaining these rewards,
we will grow in strength.

11:46.627 --> 11:49.549
So that someday, the one forcing these rules upon
the Earth... the creator-

11:50.593 --> 11:55.143
the god residing on the other side
of the book is executed!

11:55.477 --> 12:00.487
NO.005
UNITED WE NEGATE

12:01.615 --> 12:05.246
Only those seated at this Roundtable can accept quests.

12:05.623 --> 12:08.002
We need to keep a stock
of substitutes in the case of a vacancy.

12:08.378 --> 12:11.969
Leaving you two and your abilities
unchecked posed too great a risk.

12:12.427 --> 12:14.974
Especially you, Unluck.

12:15.433 --> 12:19.567
I was the one who ordered your disposal.
For that, I apologize.

12:20.318 --> 12:23.951
But I have invited you both here
on Shen’s recommendation.

12:24.284 --> 12:25.495
So I hope for your cooperation.

12:26.247 --> 12:28.459
But... like I just said, I-

12:28.544 --> 12:33.010
I see that you’re unsatisfied. In that case,
all you need to do is become number one here.

12:34.054 --> 12:38.354
Leadership of the Union is bestowed upon
the person who has achieved the most results.

12:39.064 --> 12:42.572
Work harder than me so you
can take this position from me.

12:42.822 --> 12:45.536
But wait.
Just how much... is that?

12:47.289 --> 12:48.584
Hey. You cruddy li’l book.

12:48.667 --> 12:49.878
Huh?

12:50.713 --> 12:55.514
Which one of those quests
is the hardest? C’mon, fess up!

12:55.598 --> 12:57.350
Wait, Andy!

12:57.643 --> 12:59.146
What the hell are you doing?

12:59.146 --> 13:02.612
You can’t pick a fight with Apocalypse!
Have you lost your mind?

13:08.498 --> 13:13.717
That would be Spoil, rookie.
Participant count: three. Reward is-

13:13.801 --> 13:15.679
Sick! Wicked sick!

13:16.180 --> 13:18.644
Then here’s who’s goin’-me... her...

13:19.938 --> 13:21.190
...and that damn brat over there.

13:21.273 --> 13:22.819
Me? Wait a sec,
I didn’t hear abou-

13:22.902 --> 13:24.656
Request accepted.

13:25.031 --> 13:27.578
Seriously? You gotta be kidding!

13:27.829 --> 13:30.626
Let the quest begin.

13:41.023 --> 13:43.571
AUGUST 21ST

13:43.654 --> 13:46.158
DRESSING ROOM INSIDE UNION FACILITY

13:47.411 --> 13:50.458
Uh, it’s dangerous to touch me,
so I can dress myself.

13:50.458 --> 13:53.591
These were Master Shen’s orders,
so please try to feel at ease.

13:54.133 --> 13:57.765
I am Master Shen’s subordinate, Mui.

13:57.849 --> 14:01.272
Oh, um... my name is Fuko Izumo.

14:01.272 --> 14:02.817
Yes, I am familiar.

14:02.817 --> 14:04.988
Preparations for your quest are now complete.

14:04.988 --> 14:08.704
From here on out, you are an official occupant
of the Roundtable, Miss Fuko.

14:09.204 --> 14:11.417
I wish you the best of luck on your quest.

14:12.127 --> 14:15.342
By quest, do you mean
the orders that book gave us?

14:15.425 --> 14:16.093
Indeed.

14:16.887 --> 14:19.726
Valuable rewards await you upon succeeding.

14:19.726 --> 14:22.565
Um... you’re not coming along, Ms. Mui?

14:22.649 --> 14:26.489
I’m afraid not.
I do not possess an Emblem.

14:26.573 --> 14:27.742
<i>An Emblem?</i>

14:28.242 --> 14:31.290
I am neither a Negator nor
a member of the Roundtable...

14:31.290 --> 14:35.549
...so I cannot possess an Emblem,
and thus am unauthorized to participate in quests.

14:36.760 --> 14:40.893
I implore you, Miss Fuko.
Please look after master Shen.

14:40.977 --> 14:45.068
Huh? Wait, you don’t wanna count on me.
I’m useless.

14:45.068 --> 14:47.615
Please stop bowing, Ms. Mui!

14:48.282 --> 14:51.832
<i>I see... there are people
who actually want to be Negators.</i>

14:55.338 --> 14:57.467
At least put some clothes on!

14:58.261 --> 14:59.388
Youch!

14:59.471 --> 15:00.181
Oh!

15:00.265 --> 15:00.891
Ah!

15:01.350 --> 15:01.893
Huh?

15:06.737 --> 15:08.448
Erm, so...

15:08.782 --> 15:10.828
What happened to the suit I just gave you?

15:10.828 --> 15:14.794
Burnt to ashes...
by magma that erupted outta the walls.

15:14.794 --> 15:16.715
Where in the heck is this base, anyway?

15:17.049 --> 15:22.142
All that from that little bit of contact...
I’m not a pushover... I swear I’m not a pushover.

15:23.394 --> 15:27.862
Who gives a damn ‘bout some monkey suit, anyway?
Let’s get to the quest already.

15:28.154 --> 15:31.703
This won’t do.
You need a suit, necktie, and an Emblem!

15:31.995 --> 15:32.955
And why’s that?

15:33.372 --> 15:37.590
It may look like cosplay,
but a member’s suit is actually pretty impressive.

15:37.673 --> 15:40.386
DURABILITY TEST FOOTAGE

15:40.470 --> 15:43.267
<i>The suits are bulletproof, stab-proof,
and just sturdy in general.</i>

15:43.351 --> 15:44.269
EXPERIMENT FOOTAGE

15:44.353 --> 15:47.025
<i>The necktie grants access
to any number of public services.</i>

15:47.652 --> 15:50.950
<i>It also has the ability
to translate any language.</i>

15:51.325 --> 15:54.749
<i>And the Emblem is necessary for you
to participate in quests!</i>

15:55.125 --> 15:57.630
We’ll be traveling around the world
to investigate Spoil.

15:57.713 --> 16:00.135
This gear will make for a smoother operation.

16:00.218 --> 16:03.517
Yeah, don’t need it.
I‘ll be usin’ my copter.

16:03.600 --> 16:04.226
Huh?

16:04.309 --> 16:08.777
We finally got hunters off our tail.
So me and the kid are goin’ on a date in the clouds.

16:09.486 --> 16:11.073
You’re on your own.

16:11.157 --> 16:11.783
Wait just a darn...

16:12.075 --> 16:15.123
You’re leaving me on my own?
We should move as a unit!

16:15.206 --> 16:16.710
You’ll cramp my style.
Beat it.

16:16.793 --> 16:18.129
- Aw, come on!
- Hurry up and go on. By yourself!

16:18.212 --> 16:20.049
My, what an entertaining gentleman!

16:20.133 --> 16:20.926
Why should I? No way!

16:23.932 --> 16:27.815
<i>UMA No. 1129 has taken over
a member of personnel and escaped.</i>

16:27.899 --> 16:29.611
<i>Commence capture immediately!</i>

16:29.944 --> 16:32.950
<i>UMA currently proceeding through Hall G on Level 8.</i>

16:33.242 --> 16:34.579
<i>Commence capture immediately!</i>

16:34.662 --> 16:37.042
Oh, sweet!
Time to score some points!

16:37.125 --> 16:40.340
Huh, 1129?
What level are we on?

16:40.423 --> 16:42.553
That’d be 8. Mui?

16:42.637 --> 16:45.141
Yes, sir... 1129...

16:47.647 --> 16:49.859
This is perfect timing.

16:49.859 --> 16:51.863
Number 1129.

16:51.863 --> 16:53.951
The garment UMA... Clothes.

16:54.409 --> 16:59.629
He latches onto a person’s body and transforms into
the garments that person most desires.

16:59.712 --> 17:02.635
However, once he bewitches you with those garments...

17:02.718 --> 17:05.348
...he takes total control of your body
and starts running wild.

17:06.058 --> 17:06.935
Cautionary points include-

17:07.018 --> 17:08.062
Andy! Behind you!

17:08.145 --> 17:09.273
- Stay back.
- O-Okay!

17:14.157 --> 17:16.078
We got enough problems without ya... jerk!

17:16.161 --> 17:16.871
REPAIR HEADBUTT

17:16.955 --> 17:18.709
Repair Headbutt!

17:21.171 --> 17:22.424
Looks like that hurts.

17:22.424 --> 17:25.263
I didn’t kill ‘im.
Just knocked his lights out.

17:25.514 --> 17:27.017
Oh, no. This is not good.

17:27.100 --> 17:27.893
- Huh?
- Why?

17:28.227 --> 17:32.528
When the body that 1129
has taken over loses the capacity to move...

17:32.528 --> 17:34.281
...he will seek out a new one...

17:37.454 --> 17:40.627
...and transfer himself to the nearest person.

17:40.627 --> 17:42.590
Isn’t he supposed to turn into
the clothes she wants most?

17:42.590 --> 17:44.009
I don’t see a single change.

17:44.594 --> 17:46.556
No. They’ve changed all right.

17:58.287 --> 17:59.247
Hey, Shen!

17:59.582 --> 18:01.670
Yes, Mr. Andy?

18:01.753 --> 18:04.341
Why don’t you constrict her already?

18:04.341 --> 18:07.973
My powers would work on Mui,
but Clothes doesn’t meet the requirements!

18:09.393 --> 18:12.399
These attacks are from the garments so
it’d be pointless to use my ability on her!

18:13.902 --> 18:15.572
Your power is freakin’ useless!

18:15.656 --> 18:18.745
Oh? You mean the same power that beat you?

18:18.829 --> 18:21.417
Psh, beat shmeat!
We never even finished!

18:21.417 --> 18:23.630
Aah, then how about we settle
the score after this?

18:23.630 --> 18:24.841
Bring it on!

18:26.594 --> 18:27.638
Ms. Mui.

18:28.139 --> 18:32.147
I implore you, Miss Fuko.
Please look after Master Shen.

18:40.413 --> 18:41.165
Ouch!

18:41.457 --> 18:42.125
Huh?

18:43.043 --> 18:46.551
I know we’ve only just met,
and I haven’t gotten to know you yet...

18:47.010 --> 18:51.268
...but it had to be done. I’m sorry.
This might hurt a bit. Here comes my unluck!

18:53.355 --> 18:54.692
THANK YOU Xièxiè.

18:55.401 --> 18:56.236
She’s out cold!

19:00.119 --> 19:01.371
The clothes are on the move again.

19:02.917 --> 19:07.718
<i>I knew it would come for me next.
It prefers female targets.</i>

19:14.565 --> 19:18.990
Sheesh. You took advantage
of its female preference rule, didn’tcha?

19:18.990 --> 19:23.374
Yeah, but I thought I could count on you
to come to the rescue, Andy.

19:23.792 --> 19:27.550
And even if he took control of me,
I’d be a lot easier to fight than Ms. Mui, right?

19:27.550 --> 19:30.012
You planned on unleashing that unlucky body of yours?

19:30.012 --> 19:32.016
Oh! Wait, yeah! I totally forgot!

19:32.016 --> 19:33.143
- Gimme a break.
- I mean-

19:33.227 --> 19:35.064
No better time for a spat.

19:37.736 --> 19:40.491
Master Shen, please forgive me.

19:40.951 --> 19:43.707
I’ve done a great disservice
to the one who saved my life.

19:44.082 --> 19:47.422
What are you talking about?
That was some amazing kung fu!

19:47.422 --> 19:49.467
All that daily training really paid off!

19:49.969 --> 19:54.019
Keep up the good work and you’ll be able
to do those moves on your own one day!

19:55.479 --> 19:56.899
UNDERSTOOD, SIR Zhīdàole.

19:58.444 --> 20:01.366
Oh, but what of Master Andy and Miss Fuko?

20:01.450 --> 20:04.707
Right, you see, those clothes latched on
to Mr. Andy a second ago.

20:05.124 --> 20:07.880
Huh? They aren’t turning into clothes.

20:08.506 --> 20:10.844
Damn. Damn it all!

20:10.927 --> 20:14.434
Daah! What the hell kind of desire is that?

20:14.518 --> 20:18.442
You want sturdy clothes that regenerate
when ripped and rush over when called for?

20:18.526 --> 20:19.862
Talk about a tall order!

20:20.196 --> 20:22.660
Dang, y’know,
for a UMA with clothing as their shtick...

20:22.743 --> 20:23.578
Huh?

20:23.662 --> 20:26.208
You’re lame.

20:26.918 --> 20:29.214
Oh, yeah?
I’ll show you!

20:29.297 --> 20:33.389
Once I’ve entranced you with my creation,
you’ll be my walking mannequin!

20:34.182 --> 20:37.105
Oh, yeah. The stroke of unluck
from us touching a second ago hasn’t come ye-

20:44.327 --> 20:46.916
Hey! Sorry up there!

20:48.460 --> 20:51.676
Had an Artifact malfunction!
Anybody dead?

20:52.135 --> 20:53.387
Um, well...

20:54.890 --> 20:59.023
Fifteen seconds to regenerate...
too slow. Make it faster.

20:59.107 --> 21:01.529
You’re insatiable!

21:01.612 --> 21:06.246
Nice to work with you, Mr. Clothes UMA!
Since you’re “Clothes,” I’ll call you Clothy!

21:06.329 --> 21:07.123
thy?

21:08.042 --> 21:12.341
- Well, I’ll be... they took the UMA
and made him their servant.
- That hurts, Master Shen.

21:13.177 --> 21:14.930
Well, now we’re all in proper attire.

21:15.014 --> 21:17.268
Yeah. I’m not crazy about it, though.

21:17.351 --> 21:18.437
Damn you, knock it o-

21:19.147 --> 21:23.740
<i>UMA No. 1129 has just been captured by Undead.</i>

21:23.823 --> 21:27.413
Crap! Beat to the punch!
It’s because you were too slow, Isshin!

21:28.040 --> 21:32.465
- <i>We have awarded Undead points
and promoted him to IX.</i>
- Sushi! Sushi! S-U-S-H-I!

21:33.175 --> 21:36.098
That is exactly why he was worth the wait.

21:38.143 --> 21:41.567
Mr. Nico, sir.
We have witness reports of a new UMA.

21:43.278 --> 21:48.205
We have confirmation of a rotting corpse wandering
the streets of New York.

21:48.205 --> 21:52.255
We believe this is connected
to the UMA Spoil mentioned in the quests and-

21:52.338 --> 21:57.431
Sick! I was gettin’ fed up
with how small burgers are in Japan anyway!

21:57.516 --> 22:00.062
Wha? They’re different overseas?

22:00.146 --> 22:05.072
TO BE CONTINUED

23:35.044 --> 23:36.004
PREVIEW

23:36.087 --> 23:38.968
<i>The undead and the girl head
for a town in the wastelands.</i>

23:39.302 --> 23:43.895
<i>What they saw were a group
of moaning rotten people and the plot of a young man.</i>

23:43.978 --> 23:47.527
<i>Next episode of Undead Unluck,
Episode 6-Spoil.</i>

23:47.611 --> 23:50.032
<i>In search of the greatest death ever.</i>
